{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2522","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2522","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2522\",\"parent_revision\":\"d32ecfdad6cd99a6ce8c5472e85a20afc5db887c\",\"root_revision\":\"b7616ed75a71238b1d8ce3a799c65d94d4cae888feec8c18d3a3a3bca173ff68\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAll Python packages and modules in the development-harness plugin currently live directly at the plugin root (`plugins/development-harness/`): `sam_schema/`, `backlog_core/`, `dh_config.py`, `dh_paths.py`, and newly added `dh_progressive_disclosure.py` and `progressive_markdown/`. This happened because the PEP 723 server scripts add the plugin root to `sys.path`, making imports work. That workaround became the de-facto convention. The result is a flat, disorganised root directory that mixes source packages, scripts, tests, documentation, agents, skills, and configuration with no separation.\\n\\nEvery new package added continues to pollute the root. `progressive_markdown/` and `dh_progressive_disclosure.py` were both placed there during the 2026-05-31 session, compounding the problem.\\n\\nStandard Python project layout places source packages under `src/`. The server scripts should add `src/` to `sys.path` instead of the plugin root. All existing packages (`sam_schema/`, `backlog_core/`) and utilities (`dh_config.py`, `dh_paths.py`) move to `src/`. New packages (`progressive_markdown/`) belong there too.\\n\\nThis is a prerequisite for adding further packages with proper organisation. Without it, every new addition makes the root worse.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **refactor: reorganise development-harness plugin source layout into src/ directory** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-05-31, progressive_markdown implementation exposed the problem\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-31\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-04)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n- Goal: Move all Python source packages and standalone modules from the development-harness plugin root into a `src/` subdirectory, update all `sys.path` injection sites to point at `src/` instead of the plugin root, and consolidate the four independent token-counting implementations into a single shared module.\\n- Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - Current plugin root layout confirmed: packages `sam_schema/`, `backlog_core/`, `progressive_markdown/`, `dispatch_schema/`, `agent_profile/`, standalone modules `dh_config.py`, `dh_paths.py` all live directly under `plugins/development-harness/`.\\n  - `dh_progressive_disclosure.py` already deleted (confirmed via agent memory); item description references it but it is no longer present.\\n  - All `sys.path` injection sites identified: `run_backlog_server.py` (line 27), `run_sam_server.py` (line 25), migration scripts insert `_plugin_root` or `_HARNESS_DIR`.\\n  - `pyproject.toml` pytest `pythonpath` and `[tool.ty] extra-paths` both add `./plugins/development-harness` \u2014 must be updated to `./plugins/development-harness/src`.\\n  - Token-counting duplication confirmed at four locations: `backlog_core/server.py` (`_enc` + `_token_count()`), `sam_schema/server.py` (`_enc`), `progressive_markdown/list_navigator.py` (`ENCODING`), `progressive_markdown/tokenizer.py` (`TokenBudgeter`).\\n  - `TokenBudgeter` is the highest-quality implementation (count, fits, split_to_budget, truncate_to_budget with binary search).\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - `dispatch_schema/` and `agent_profile/` are Python packages at the plugin root not mentioned in item description \u2014 scope should include them. Derivable from directory inspection.\\n  - Standard Python `src/` layout uses no `__init__.py` in the `src/` directory itself.\\n  - Shared token-counting module target: `plugins/development-harness/src/dh_tokenizer.py` alongside `dh_config.py` and `dh_paths.py`.\\n- MISSING:\\n  - No explicit decision on whether `dispatch_schema/` and `agent_profile/` are in scope or deferred.\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Refactor\\n- Behavioral boundary: MCP server scripts launch without ImportError; all existing tests pass after the move; all import paths resolve from `src/`.\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: Import correctness under the new path \u2014 not that files were moved, but that every consumer (server scripts, test runner, migration scripts, `ty`, `ruff`) resolves the packages from `src/` and no `ImportError` occurs.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Every new package added to the plugin compounds root pollution. Without this, the convention is unenforced and the root grows with each feature. Prerequisite for clean package addition going forward.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Any new Python package added to development-harness continues to land at the plugin root until this is done.\\n- Bottleneck: Flat root mixes source, agents, skills, scripts, tests, docs \u2014 no separation visible to contributors.\\n- High blast radius: server scripts, all migration scripts, test runner config (`pyproject.toml` `pythonpath`), type checker config (`ty.extra-paths`), and token-counting consumers all require coordinated updates.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Source packages separated from agents, skills, scripts, tests, documentation, and configuration.\\n- `src/` layout creates an enforced boundary: new packages must be placed under `src/` for imports to work.\\n- Token-counting consolidation removes three redundant tiktoken encoder instances and one duplicate binary-search implementation.\\n- Future packages have an obvious, discoverable home.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter the refactor:\\n\\n- `uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` starts without error; `backlog_list` responds correctly.\\n- `uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_server.py` starts without error; `sam_list` responds correctly.\\n- `uv run pytest` suite passes with zero new failures.\\n- All `sys.path.insert` calls in server scripts inject `_plugin_root / \\\"src\\\"` instead of `_plugin_root`.\\n- Token count calls in `backlog_core/server.py` and `sam_schema/server.py` use the shared `dh_tokenizer` module rather than maintaining independent `_enc` instances.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n```text\\nplugins/development-harness/\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 agent_profile/\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 backlog_core/\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 dispatch_schema/\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 progressive_markdown/\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 sam_schema/\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 dh_config.py\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 dh_paths.py\\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 dh_tokenizer.py   <- new shared token-counting module\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 scripts/              (unchanged; sys.path patched to insert src/)\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests_sam/\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 agents/\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 skills/\\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 docs/\\n```\\n\\nEach `sys.path.insert` changes from `str(_plugin_root)` to `str(_plugin_root / \\\"src\\\")`.\\n\\n`pyproject.toml` `pythonpath` entry `./plugins/development-harness` changes to `./plugins/development-harness/src`. Same for `[tool.ty] extra-paths`.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` starts and `backlog_list` tool responds without error (verifiable via `fastmcp call`).\\n2. `uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_server.py` starts and `sam_list` tool responds without error.\\n3. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests` passes with zero failures and zero collection errors after the move.\\n4. `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/src/` exits 0 \u2014 no new linting errors.\\n5. `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/src/` exits 0 (or with only pre-existing warnings) \u2014 no new type errors from import path changes.\\n6. The packages `backlog_core`, `sam_schema`, `dispatch_schema`, `agent_profile`, `progressive_markdown` and modules `dh_config.py`, `dh_paths.py` are absent from `plugins/development-harness/` at root level \u2014 they exist only under `plugins/development-harness/src/`.\\n7. `grep -r \\\"tiktoken.get_encoding\\\" plugins/development-harness/src/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/src/sam_schema/server.py` returns zero matches \u2014 both servers delegate to the shared `dh_tokenizer` module.\\n8. All migration scripts (`migrate_plan_artifacts.py`, `migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py`, `dh_migrate.py`, `verify_migration_fidelity.py`, `close_test_issues.py`) execute without `ImportError`.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` lines 24-28 \u2014 sys.path injection pattern |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_server.py` lines 23-26 \u2014 sys.path injection pattern |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/progressive_markdown/tokenizer.py` \u2014 TokenBudgeter, authoritative token-counting implementation |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` lines 77-80 \u2014 `_token_count()` and `_enc` to be replaced |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` line 166 \u2014 `_enc` to be replaced |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/progressive_markdown/list_navigator.py` line 42 \u2014 `ENCODING` to be replaced |\\n| Config | `pyproject.toml` line 426 `pythonpath` and line 62 `ty.extra-paths` \u2014 both add plugin root, must change to `src/` |\\n| Agent memory | `plugins/development-harness/.claude/agent-memory/python-engineering-python-cli-architect/project_progressive_markdown.md` \u2014 confirms dh_progressive_disclosure.py was deleted |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: Any future package addition to development-harness that should live in `src/`\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Scope ambiguity: `dispatch_schema/` and `agent_profile/` are Python packages at the plugin root not mentioned in the item description. Confirm whether they are in scope (recommended) or intentionally deferred.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 The file moves are mechanical; the risk is high blast radius. Server scripts, migration scripts, test runner configuration, type-checker config, and token-counting consolidation are all coordinated changes. Token-counting consolidation adds moderate implementation complexity (new shared module, update two servers, verify no behaviour change). Estimated 2-4 hours with validation at each step.\\n\",\"digest\":\"e9baaf5ed47a549dc480e9afe8ca4223cf318be8d1f494ffa391a3939ee140ac\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnMEVA\"}"}